  Version 1 anchored on the MEDIAN. That was void: a fit that has learned
  nothing sits at the MODE, which v1 scored as maximal learning.

====================================================================================================
2.1  ARD SEPARATION vs ITS OWN NO-SIGNAL NULL   <-- THE DECIDING STATISTIC
====================================================================================================
The prior is identical on every dimension, so ANY uninformed fit — prior-
dominated, badly initialised, whatever — gives inert/active = 1.00 by
symmetry. Measured on permuted outcomes the null is 1.11 at n=46. Anything
above that is data-driven discrimination and cannot be an artefact of the
anchoring error that voided version 1.

